      DependencyIndex: 27
      LevelID: 28
      NodeType: 3
      Ports:
        Description:
          String: ""
        DescriptionText:
          ClassType1: TEXT
          String: |-
            Hue/Saturation lets you adjust the hue,  saturation,  and lightness of the overall image. 
            
            Hue - The values reflect the number of degrees of rotation around the wheel from the original color of the pixel.  A positive value indicates clockwise rotation,  and a negative value,  counterclockwise rotation.  Values can range from ‑180 to +180.
            Saturation - The color shifts away from or toward the center of the color wheel.  Values can range from ‑100 (percentage of desaturation) to +100 (percentage of saturation increase).
            Lightness - For Lightness,  enter a value or drag the slider to the right to increase the lightness or to the left to decrease it.  Values can range from ‑100 to +100.
        FirstTime:
          Variable: false
        Locked:
          Variable: false
        SubGraphUniqueID29:
          Connection0:
            NodeLevelID: 26
            PortID: Output
